        "calls": 1,
        "title": "Desktop fork support for worktree chats in cloud contracts",
        "summary": "The shared desktop-cloud contracts in `common` now allow forking a chat that runs in its own worktree, not just shared or local chats. The `CloudHistoryChatFork` type gains a `cutAtTurn` field, mirroring `CloudHistorySideChat`, and its `into` parameter makes `projectId` optional for forks that stay in the worktree. The `HostedWorkspaceHost` interface adds a `worktreeFork` capability flag and a `fork` field on the `runtime` method's scope, which is answered in the `forked` response of the same request.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "maintainers",
        "evidence": "In `common/src/desktop-cloud/history.ts`, `CloudHistoryChatFork` adds a `cutAtTurn` field and makes `into`'s `projectId` optional. In `common/src/desktop-cloud/hosted-workspace.ts`, `HostedWorkspaceHost` adds the `worktreeFork` capability flag and a `fork` field to the `runtime` method's scope.",
