        "calls": 1,
        "title": "CLI model availability notice now hidden for full access and paid",
        "summary": "The CLI chat header now calls the new `getFreebuffSessionModelAvailabilityNotice` helper, which returns the model availability line only when a session is at limited access, has no subscription tier or Freebucks plan, and carries reason fields. Previously, the header rendered the generic fallback for every response lacking a reason, including full-access and paid-plan accounts, which incorrectly implied a network problem. The shared `common` package also rewords that generic fallback from a connection-specific phrase to a neutral availability statement. Two other changes accompany the logic update: updated doc comments clarifying the new gating behavior, and new unit tests verifying that paid plans, full-access overrides, and refusals suppress the notice.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "end-users",
        "evidence": "cli/src/components/freebuff-chat-header.tsx now imports and calls getFreebuffSessionModelAvailabilityNotice instead of getFreebuffModelAvailabilityNotice; common/src/util/freebuff-model-availability.ts adds this new exported function that gates on access tier and plan, and changes the generic fallback string from 'Some models aren't available on this connection' to 'Some models aren't available yet'.",
